./xmodel/max12-812-order4-residual-cusp-kummer-genus1-review-grok-20260826.log:4:**Unconditional plane theorem holds.** Newton polygon `conv{(0,0),(0,2),(1,3),(8,3)}` has area `23/2`, boundary `11`, seven interior points. `P` is geometrically irreducible (Ostrowski: the hull is Minkowski-indecomposable). Length four plus Hessian unit gives four ordinary torus nodes over the algebraic closure. Membership is containment only, not dominance. The point at `q=-4/27` is one `(2,7)` cusp, delta three, `ord(v)=-6`, not two branches of order `-3`. Then `g(X)=7-4-3=0`, `div(v)=8P_0-P_{ul}-P_A-6P_B`, and Riemann–Hurwitz for `y^4=v` gives `g(Y)=1`. The nondegenerate genera `7/37/165` are not used.
