./xmodel/as-fonly-p3-balanced-cyclotomic-terminal-family-review-grok-20260824.md:184:`Q_m` has integer coefficients. For `P_m`, write `2k+1=3^a u` with `u` coprime to 3. Then `2k+1>=3^a`, so `k>=(3^a-1)/2`. The comparison `a<=(3^a-1)/2` is `3^a>=2a+1`, which holds for every `a>=0`. Hence `a<=k`, and after cancelling `3^a` the remaining denominator is the unit `u`. Every coefficient of `P_m` therefore lies in `Z_{(3)} subset Z_3`. Direct 3-adic valuation for `k=0..400` never violates `v_3(2k+1)<=k`. Equality `v_3(2k+1)=k` occurs only at `(k,2k+1)=(0,1)` and `(1,3)`.
